    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Arctic-midlatitude climate linkages",
    "problem": "Large uncertainties persist regarding the influence of Arctic amplification on mid-latitude weather due to incomplete knowledge of dynamical processes, sparse and short data records, and imperfect climate models.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a synthesis where reduced Arctic sea ice and extensive Eurasian snow cover constructively interfere to force a planetary wave pattern that weakens the polar vortex, leading to cold and severe winter weather across mid-latitude continents.",
    "task": "The task is to review and synthesize the current understanding of potential dynamical pathways that link rapid Arctic warming (Arctic amplification) and the loss of sea ice and snow cover to the increasing frequency of extreme weather events in the mid-latitudes.",
